{"questions":[{"question_id":"NsCYJitWTAAPyjgQ","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline","year":2013,"examDate":2013,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"biomolecules","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","topic":"vitamins-and-nucleic-acids","type":"integer","marks":4,"negMarks":0,"permalink":"the-total-number-of-lone-pairs-of-electrons-in-melamine-is-2013-marks-4-nscyjitwtaapyjgq.htm","content":"The total number of lone-pairs of electrons in melamine is","options":[],"correct_options":[],"explanation":"<p>The structure of melamine is :</p>\n\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1lyinxqg5/4fc20537-fc09-4d00-b4d7-9d78f91c3065/b0a21550-4048-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinxqg6.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1lyinxqg5/4fc20537-fc09-4d00-b4d7-9d78f91c3065/b0a21550-4048-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinxqg6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Biomolecules Question 24 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1lyinxqg5/4fc20537-fc09-4d00-b4d7-9d78f91c3065/b0a21550-4048-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinxqg6.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1lyinxqg5/4fc20537-fc09-4d00-b4d7-9d78f91c3065/b0a21550-4048-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinxqg6.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1lyinxqg5/4fc20537-fc09-4d00-b4d7-9d78f91c3065/b0a21550-4048-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinxqg6.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1lyinxqg5/4fc20537-fc09-4d00-b4d7-9d78f91c3065/b0a21550-4048-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinxqg6.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1lyinxqg5/4fc20537-fc09-4d00-b4d7-9d78f91c3065/b0a21550-4048-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinxqg6.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1lyinxqg5/4fc20537-fc09-4d00-b4d7-9d78f91c3065/b0a21550-4048-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinxqg6.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n<p>Each nitrogen has one lone pair of electrons. Number (no.) of nitrogen in a molecule $=6$</p>\n\n<p>Total no. of lone pairs in melamine</p>\n\n<p>$$ \\begin{aligned} &amp; =\\text { No. of nitrogen } \\times \\text { lone pair } \\\\\\\\ &amp; =6 \\times 1=6 \\end{aligned} $$</p>\n\n<p>Hence, total number of lone pair on nitrogen is 6.</p>"}]}